  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10a-2024-p1.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Just compute each piece. We have \\(9901 \\cdot 101 = 990100 + 9901\\) \\(= 1000001,\\) and \\(99 \\cdot 10101 = 999999.\\) Subtracting, \\(1000001 - 999999 = 2.\\) Thus, A is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "Expand each product by writing \\(101 = 100 + 1\\) and \\(10101 = 10000 + 100 + 1\\)",
        "Both products are very close to \\(10^6;\\) compute each and subtract"
      ],
